  "notes": [
    "A checkout is one order plus its line items, and WaveDB has no multi-record transaction: each record is its own atomic batch. The durable row makes the whole checkout durable once, at its end (RFC 0072) — one barrier, as the other four commit once.",
    "Retains every superseded version; the other four retain none. Read the write phases beside the footprint, never alone.",
    "Measured on the RFC 0065 producer/consumer harness: `wall_ns` is the phase's wall clock, `total_ns` is the sum of the timed windows, and the percentiles are pooled across every consumer. Read counters are absent (phase 4)."
  ]
